	* : feature-scda: Introduce two versions of fixed padding  As
	announced in the commit description of db724acb we add the analogous
	changes for the fixed-length paddding.

2024-08-21  Tim Griesbach <tim.griesbach@uni-bonn.de>

	* : feature-scda: Introduce two versions of mod padding  Since we do
	not want to copy the potentially very big data, we also offer a
	padding function that only sets the padding bytes but does not copy
	the input data. For the fixed-length padding the data sizes are
	smaller and known in advance. That is why, we prefer the inplace
	padding for the fixed-length padding. However, for the sakes of
	flexibility and symmetry we will also add non-inplace function for
